%description:
Tests the TS option on the RST of a user abort (RFC 7323 section 5.2: "If an
<RST> is being generated because of a user abort, and Snd.TS.OK is set, then a
Timestamps option SHOULD be included in the <RST>"). The client aborts at
t=2 s; its RST carries TSecr 0, because it has no ACK bit (section 3.2).

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 100"
*.cli_app.tAbort=2s
*.*_tcp.timestampSupport = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1:101(100) ack 501 win 16384   Option(s): NOP NOP TS(1000,2)
[1.203 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 101 win 16384   Option(s): NOP NOP TS(1202,1000)
cli_tcp: ESTABLISHED --> CLOSED  (on ABORT)
[2.001 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: R win 0   Option(s): NOP NOP TS(2000,0)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
